; metacalc Z80 canvas for the TI-84 Plus SE. Draws into a 96 by 64 frame buffer in RAM that
; matches crates/mcui/src/canvas.rs, and copies it to the LCD. Nothing else draws.
;
; Code runs from flash and is position dependent. Assembling this file alone places it at
; $4000; an including file defines UI_EMBEDDED first and places the code itself. The glyph
; table is generated: `mcglyph z80 font.inc`, found through the include path as "font.inc".
;
; RAM, two blocks that default to space TI-OS leaves to an app and can be moved with UI_FRAME
; and UI_VARS: the frame, 768 bytes at UI_FRAME, default $9340 (plotSScreen), row-major, 12
; bytes a row, the most significant bit leftmost; and UI_VARS_SIZE ($1A, 26) bytes of variables
; at UI_VARS, default $9882 (appBackUpScreen + $10), laid out in ram.inc. The blocks must not
; overlap. Call ui_set_font and ui_clear before the first draw. Registers not listed as
; destroyed are preserved, and IX, IY and the shadow registers are never touched. The stack
; needs 12 bytes.
;
; Fonts: every routine that draws or measures text reads the table given to ui_set_font. A
; table is what mcglyph z80 writes: a slot of 8 bytes per glyph, the width then seven row
; bytes; a glyph nine wide takes a second slot of its ninth pixels. Strings are glyph codes
; ended by 0 and code 1 is the space. The soft key row sets ui_key_font itself.
;
; Text rows are 0 to 7 and eight scanlines each; a glyph's seven rows start one scanline
; below the top. Pixels outside the frame are dropped as the model drops them. Truncating,
; wrapping and folding are decided by the caller.
;
; Routines (details at each): ui_set_font, ui_clear, ui_text, ui_text_width, ui_text_right,
; ui_text_centered, ui_invert, ui_invert_row, ui_marker, ui_title, ui_list_row, ui_soft_keys,
; ui_blit. ui_blit waits on the busy flag, bit 7 of port 10h, before every LCD write
; and leaves the controller in 8 bit mode with increment mode 5, as TI-OS expects it.

#ifndef UI_EMBEDDED
.org $4000
#endif

#include "ram.inc"
#include "glyph.inc"
#include "shapes.inc"
#include "bars.inc"
#include "blit.inc"
#include "font.inc"
